# Results. Every arm writes to its own results/ beside its scripts. New files there are
# ignored; the nine committed before this rule (the June CITE-seq outputs, the Kang markers,
# de_metrics_mu10_nobatch.csv) stay tracked, so `git status` shows them if a run rewrites them.
*/results/
# Scratch from earlier verification sessions, not arm results.
output/

# Experiment inputs, fetched or derived rather than committed. decision-data-out-of-head
# has fetch_data.py rebuild this from data_sources.yaml.
data/
*/data/
!*/legacy/data/
!nullsplit/data/
!citeseq/data/

# The CITE-seq rebuild chain's artifacts, ~80 MB per run. citeseq/data/ is
# un-ignored above so memory_CD4.h5ad can stay committed, which also exposes the
# 29 MB raw download fetch_data puts beside it -- hence naming it explicitly.
citeseq/data/sc5p_v2_hs_PBMC_10k_filtered_feature_bc_matrix.h5
citeseq/R/Rplots.pdf

# Local caches used to keep Numba/Matplotlib writable under sandboxing
.numba_cache/
.mpl_cache/

# Temp config used to point clustering/metrics.py at the DE-results h5ad
.metrics_config.yaml
